# Generated and locked files. Marking them keeps them collapsed in GitHub's
# diff view and skipped by review tooling, so a pull request shows the change a
# person made rather than the build output that followed from it.
#
# `register/releases/` is deliberately NOT marked. A dated edition's payload is
# git-ignored, so the only committed file there is its `manifest.json` -- and a
# change to one of those is an edition changing identity, which is exactly what
# a reviewer has to see rather than have folded away.
*.lock linguist-generated=true
register/tapio_register/generated/** linguist-generated=true
